  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Police used batons and pepper spray on far-right protesters in Portsmouth unrest",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/sep/07/police-used-batons-and-pepper-spray-on-far-right-protesters-in-portsmouth-unrest",
      "description": "<p>Minister condemns groups behind Hampshire disorder and says officers were injured as they repelled ‘aggression’</p><p>Batons and synthetic pepper spray were used to repel hundreds of masked, black-clad vigilantes in Portsmouth on Sunday, it has emerged, as the policing minister said officers had been injured as they repelled organised “aggression”.</p><p>After police contained the weekend’s second disruptive demonstration against asylum seekers travelling to the UK in small boats, it was claimed that officers in Hampshire were pushed off their motorbikes and pelted with bricks. Sarah Jones, the Home Office minister, condemned groups behind the disorder for promoting “racism and thuggery”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/sep/07/police-used-batons-and-pepper-spray-on-far-right-protesters-in-portsmouth-unrest\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-07T19:12:16"
    },
    {
      "title": "No 10 condemns ‘thuggish’ far-right activists after Portsmouth unrest",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/sep/07/ministers-condemn-far-right-activists-portsmouth-asylum-seekers",
      "description": "<p>Hundreds of men, some in balaclavas, try to prevent asylum seekers’ processing, two days after similar scenes in Dover</p><p>Downing Street has condemned the “thuggish and intimidating behaviour” of far-right activists <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/sep/06/far-right-protesters-descend-on-portsmouth-after-small-boat-arrival\">who blocked roads</a> in Portsmouth when a boat carrying asylum seekers arrived in the city, two days <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/sep/05/black-clad-protesters-balaclavas-block-road-port-of-dover-kent\">after similar scenes</a> in Dover.</p><p>Hundreds of men, some dressed in black and wearing balaclavas, tried to stop the arrivals from being transported for processing until 3am, when police removed them with threats of arrest.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/sep/07/ministers-condemn-far-right-activists-portsmouth-asylum-seekers\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-07T15:34:00"
    }
  ]
